# critical-services.conf — allowlist of systemd units "I care about".
#
# Used by TWO components:
#   1. critical-services-check.sh (watchdog, timer every 60s)
#      → pages CRITICAL when a listed unit is not in 'active' state,
#        emits CLEAR on recovery. Catches long outages; may miss
#        fast restarts (< 60s) due to poll cadence.
#   2. lifecycle-watcher.sh (tails systemd journal, real-time)
#      → fires WARNING on every Started / Stopped transition of a
#        listed unit. Catches restarts of any duration.
#
# One unit per line. Lines starting with # and blank lines are ignored.
# Absent file or empty allowlist ⇒ both components silently no-op.
# After editing, the watchdog picks changes up on the next 60s tick;
# the lifecycle-watcher picks them up within one event.
#
# Uncomment + edit per host:
# nginx.service
# postgresql.service
# docker.service
# redis-server.service
